{"title":"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(General_Method)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (General Method)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many numbers are in the finite sequence of consecutive perfect squares <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/f/01f9f1e62863b82d5548bc8d8a32e611c94449ca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9, 16, 25, \\ldots , 2500?\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"16\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The perfect squares are from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/9/819068968ed60608a91d0c3921d6296964660e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/a/46a6d5052d1de3dbed09284a27ab36f429a43655.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50^2$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore, the answer is the amount of positive integers between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, inclusive. This is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/9/a09229ad48714b144c644d574345f0d94bc16ddb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50-3+1=\\boxed{48}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"136\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28General_Method.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(General_Method)\">Solution 2 (General Method)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (General Method)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The set is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae9b3741279b2ae9404f386ce2d7dff0a48fc797.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S=\\{3^2,4^2,5^2,\\cdots,50^2\\}\\]\" width=\"188\" height=\"20\" />\nNotice that the cardinality of\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/d/90d5c46dd980b3c511c9a6bcbcdb8b55975114a9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\{a_1,a_2,\\cdots,a_n\\}\\]\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />\nis equal to the cardinality of\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/8/6b85b228b9cf42b9192652ead773eda4cf7d9b72.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\{f(a_1),f(a_2),\\cdots, f(a_n)\\}\\]\" width=\"195\" height=\"18\" />\nFor all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> with domain containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/917856f3e47dd4905417192594ce27d9967d21d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, \\cdots, a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"78\" height=\"11\" />. \nIn our case, apply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/6/ba6133cf3e9c6d0a14d7e5e86194a8087cc5d9f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=\\sqrt{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"19\" /> to get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/6/3361045d0f611194925b6692560f262500e7d68c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S_1=\\{3,4,5,\\cdots,50\\}\\]\" width=\"164\" height=\"18\" />\nNow apply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c5421901ac0bc15e7a32618f2ee7555449c0def6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=x-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" /> to get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/3/bc333d6c06a8b6783bf6b1bf441eefd788c5ccfc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S_2=\\{1,2,3,\\cdots,48\\}\\]\" width=\"164\" height=\"18\" />\nWhich clearly has cardinality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/8/0f8237986dfc7b48f5742811852533ca254b06c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{48}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~yofro\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ol><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems\">Other 2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Answer Key\">2021 JMPSC Sprint Answer Key</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JMPSC_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"JMPSC Problems and Solutions\">All JMPSC Problems and Solutions</a></li></ol>\n<p>The problems on this page are copyrighted by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://jmpsc.org\">Junior Mathematicians' Problem Solving Competition</a>. <span class=\"mw-valign-middle\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:JMPSC.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/120px-JMPSC.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"120\" height=\"120\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/180px-JMPSC.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/a/ab/JMPSC.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018020032\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.040 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 94/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 183/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2809/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.204      1 Template:JMPSC_Notice\n100.00%    5.204      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21610:|#|:idhash:canonical and t